{"text":"And I know things, how gray webs sketched the cool thread strung by slave ships, how the wet in a child's house for birds calls pink slugs. The ants, the dark, the web, the green mold are not at war, no, but they are in it, and so am I. The round bulge on the side of the tree makes her look like she's with child. I take three steps, and the mound is now two butt cheeks. Four more steps, and it, two skin folds like the heat of a mist. A smile, step, it's a heart, and now a child wants more. I want one, but I am one, all this throb, all wait, breaths a long dead dash as we pray to be left to our own. So I watch paints flew wood for earth like seeds, blue rolls off, the brown creeps in like dew on a rag. I stare in the house I made for birds, and I think I might sing. I gulp it down, but not all of it.","words":[{"text":"And","start":0.0,"end":0.62},{"text":"I","start":0.62,"end":0.78},{"text":"know","start":0.78,"end":1.04},{"text":"things","start":1.04,"end":1.58,"punct":","},{"text":"how","start":1.68,"end":2.06},{"text":"gray","start":2.06,"end":2.56},{"text":"webs","start":2.56,"end":2.92},{"text":"sketched","start":2.92,"end":3.48},{"text":"the","start":3.48,"end":3.64},{"text":"cool","start":3.64,"end":3.9},{"text":"thread","start":3.9,"end":4.28},{"text":"strung","start":4.28,"end":4.8},{"text":"by","start":4.8,"end":5.18},{"text":"slave","start":5.18,"end":5.56},{"text":"ships","start":5.56,"end":6.04,"punct":","},{"text":"how","start":6.06,"end":6.6},{"text":"the","start":6.6,"end":6.8},{"text":"wet","start":6.8,"end":7.08},{"text":"in","start":7.08,"end":7.46},{"text":"a","start":7.46,"end":7.56},{"text":"child's","start":7.56,"end":8.08},{"text":"house","start":8.08,"end":8.34},{"text":"for","start":8.34,"end":8.58},{"text":"birds","start":8.58,"end":8.96},{"text":"calls","start":8.96,"end":9.3},{"text":"pink","start":9.3,"end":9.78},{"text":"slugs","start":9.78,"end":10.44,"punct":"."},{"text":"The","start":11.06,"end":11.26},{"text":"ants","start